Knowledge Check (3 Questions):

Question 1: What is the difference between stack and heap memory in Java?


Stack stores primitives only; Heap stores objects


Stack stores local variables and method calls; Heap stores all objects


Heap is faster than stack


Stack is used for garbage collection


Answer: B Explanation: Stack memory is allocated per thread for local variables and method execution. Heap is shared and stores all objects. Stack is automatically freed when methods exit; Heap is managed by garbage collector.
Question 2: What will this code print?
String result = switch("JAVA") {
    case "JAVA" -&gt; "Programming Language";
    case "SQL" -&gt; "Query Language";
    default -&gt; "Unknown";
};
System.out.println(result);


Programming Language


Query Language


Unknown


Compilation Error


Answer: A Explanation: Switch expression matches “JAVA” with first case and returns “Programming Language”.
